# Architecture & system design

Full ADRs live in `AGENTS.md`. Do not contradict them without an explicit human-approved ADR update.

## Locked choices

| Area | Decision |
|------|----------|
| Layout | `mobile/`, `backend/`, `docs/` |
| Backend lang | TypeScript only |
| Migrations | Knex (SQL-friendly MVP) |
| Flutter state | Riverpod only |
| Flutter shape | Feature-first + presentation/domain/data |
| API | REST `/api/v1`, layers: routes→controllers→services→repositories |
| Auth | Email/username+password + Google; no public signup; JWT access+refresh |
| Shops | `shop_id` required on shop data from day one |
| Stock | Single TX: lock → update qty → insert history |
| Errors | `{ error: { code, message, details } }` |
| Reports | `exceljs` + `pdfkit` in services |
| Deploy | Local-first; no microservices/queues in V1 |

## DO / DON'T

```text
✅ Put business rules in services / domain
✅ Filter by shop_id from auth context
❌ Fat controllers with SQL
❌ Client-trusted role/shop_id for authz
❌ Offline sync frameworks in V1
❌ Second state-management library beside Riverpod
```

Changing a locked decision → update `AGENTS.md` ADR first, then code.
